    "prompt": "Create an ORIGINAL complete hand-painted 2D sprite master sheet for a CHEMTECH DRAKE neutral creature for original Heroes of Might and Magic III visual aesthetics, Runeterra-inspired. EXACT 4 columns by 4 rows,16 separated complete whole-body poses, constant body scale,equal cells,huge clear transparent gutters. True transparent background. Every wingtip,tailtip,horn and foot unclipped. SAME character facing RIGHT in low three-quarter HoMM3 battlefield view, upper-left soft light. Living adult WYVERN, two powerful hindlegs plus a pair of wing forelimbs. Broad muscular olive-grey scaled chest, short bull-like dragon muzzle, two backward charcoal horns, cropped thorn ridge, pale ochre belly, long muscular tapering tail. Large ragged but viable membranous wings with deep green leathery membranes. Chemtech adaptation: two modest cylindrical tarnished brass pressure tanks strapped firmly behind shoulders, clearly readable short curved ribbed hoses from these tanks around neck to a metal jaw respirator and reinforced wing-wrist bracers. Hoses contain tiny lime-green liquid accents, restrained green eye, visibly biological dragon not metal robot. Matte textured pebbled scales and aged bronze, strong heavy predatory silhouette. Not Hextech, no blue crystals or mechanical dinosaur. Textured finished painted2D, convincing anatomy, restrained highlights matched to native originalHoMM3 Griffin materials, no3Drender,glossyfigurine,photorealisticflesh,anime,vectoroutlines or blurryhaze. No aura, gas cloud, breath, projectile, crest,text, grid,castshadow. ROW1 four GROUNDED holding breathing poses,wings folded,hindclaws planted. ROW2 four AIRBORNE FLIGHT wingbeats ordered fullyup,strongdownstroke,fullydown,recoveryupstroke,feet visibly tucked and off ground. ROW3 four TAKEOFF poses:crouch,unfurlwings,hindlegspring,airborne wingbeat. ROW4 four LANDING poses:airborneapproach,wingflare,clawstouchdown,wingsfoldgrounded. Real distinct joint articulation, do not repeat one pose. Complete dragons centered inside generous cells, separate empty transparent gutters.\n",
